Here Image does not mean a photo or picture. 🙂

In AWS SageMaker, Image = the preconfigured software environment used to run your JupyterLab space.

| Setting                                 | Meaning                                                   |
| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Instance: `ml.t3.medium`**            | The cloud computer hardware — CPU and RAM                 |
| **Image: SageMaker Distribution 3.0.0** | The software environment installed on that cloud computer |


===

Think of it like your laptop:

Instance  = Computer hardware 💻
             ↓
          CPU + RAM

Image     = Software environment 🖥️
             ↓
          OS + Python + Jupyter + Libraries

====

Simple example

When you click Run space:

AWS Instance
ml.t3.medium
2 vCPU + 4 GB RAM
        +
SageMaker Image
Distribution 3.0.0
        ↓
JupyterLab starts
        ↓
You can run Python / ML code

=====

So, Instance decides the power of the computer

while Image decides the software environment running inside it.

=====

For your current SageMaker learning, you can keep the default:

Instance: ml.t3.medium
Image: SageMaker Distribution 3.0.0


